v
 A test, and the suite that survives deleting the kitchen sink. Nothing names
 this file: make test hands every tests/*.b98 to cfunge in turn and reads the
 TAP each one prints, so a test file is found by existing. Run them all with
 make test.
 
 Befunge has no test framework and no way to write one, because it has no
 functions -- so a test here is a program that prints TAP and exits with the
 number of assertions that failed. The 1..2 two rows below is the plan, and
 adding an assertion means changing that number by hand: nothing counts for
 you, and a plan that disagrees with the ok lines is a failure of its own.
 
 An assertion is arithmetic rather than a call. Each row leaves a flag, !!
 normalises it to 0 or 1, and that one flag does two jobs: it is added to the
 failure count, and multiplied by 4 it tells j how many cells to skip. The
 four cells in question are $ drops, and what they drop is the not at the
 front of the message -- so one string prints ok when the test passed and
 not ok when it did not. The text in the quotes is the name of the test, and
 it is what a failure shows you, so write it to read on its own.
 
 The running count lives in the cell at 0,-1, one row above the playfield.
 That is deliberate: a cell inside the grid is a cell this file might grow
 into, and the kitchen sink beside this one records the time that happened.
 01-0p writes it, 01-0g reads it, and the last row exits with it.
>001-0p                                                                       v
v"1..2"0<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<
>>:#,_a,$                                                                     v
v"not ok 1 - a string pushed left to right comes back off right to left"0<<<<<<
>"Hi"$88*8+-!!:01-0g+01-0p4*j$$$$>:#,_a,$                                     v
v"not ok 2 - the zero under a string is what stops the printing loop"0<<<<<<<<<
>0"Hi"$$0-!!:01-0g+01-0p4*j$$$$>:#,_a,$                                       v
v<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<
>01-0gq
